From 2ec6463c9f9c122af3e3f5bb8eebfeb9acbe1d7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: r2d2 <r2d2@localhost>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 15:23:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] injection_points: add planner path-prune notice action

Add a test action for the planner path-pruning injection points.  It emits
one NOTICE line per event using simple key=value fields: path type, index
oid where one applies, costs, row estimate, pathkeys and required_outer for
both the new path and the one responsible for the decision.

The existing "notice" action treats the injection point argument as a
string, so attaching it to a point that passes a typed payload prints
garbage; this action understands the payload instead.

Two details are worth noting.  Upper relations have no relids, so they are
reported as "upper" rather than as an empty set that would look like a
relation.  Bitmap paths are attributed to the index of their bitmap qual,
because otherwise a displacement between two paths over the same physical
index appears to involve no index at all.

The row estimate is included because it is what most clearly separates two
candidates over the same index: an unparameterized path over a large table
and a parameterized one differ by orders of magnitude in rows while sharing
the same index oid.

This is a test helper, not a planner reporting API.
